1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,261
The bus stand Chai Corner
is packed every morning.

2
00:00:03,561 --> 00:00:06,361
Meena runs it, but she
needs two more helpers.

3
00:00:06,912 --> 00:00:10,041
Last year, Ravi hired the
first person who asked.

4
00:00:10,341 --> 00:00:13,533
That helper came late, burnt
the milk, and quit in a week.

5
00:00:13,833 --> 00:00:16,557
This time, Ravi cannot
afford a wrong pick.

6
00:00:17,207 --> 00:00:18,883
More hands are not enough.

7
00:00:18,883 --> 00:00:20,558
He needs the right people.

8
00:00:21,258 --> 00:00:22,425
This is staffing.

9
00:00:22,775 --> 00:00:25,586
At Chai Corner, Asha
trains every new helper.

10
00:00:25,936 --> 00:00:27,839
That is part of staffing too.

11
00:00:27,839 --> 00:00:31,110
Staffing means filling every
job with the right person.

12
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:35,041
And keeping it filled, because
people leave, grow, and move up.

13
00:00:35,691 --> 00:00:37,562
Staffing runs in eight steps.

14
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:40,057
Plan, recruit, select, and place.

15
00:00:40,407 --> 00:00:42,860
Then train, appraise, promote, and pay.

16
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:45,535
Let's watch Ravi run the first four.

17
00:00:46,135 --> 00:00:47,035
Step one.

18
00:00:46,959 --> 00:00:48,235
Manpower planning.

19
00:00:48,235 --> 00:00:50,505
How many people, and what kind?

20
00:00:50,855 --> 00:00:52,420
Meena needs two helpers.

21
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:55,430
One for the tea, one for
cups and the counter.

22
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:56,680
Step two.

23
00:00:56,665 --> 00:00:57,647
Recruitment.

24
00:00:57,647 --> 00:00:59,804
Getting good people to apply.

25
00:01:00,154 --> 00:01:04,389
A notice on the stall, and a word
from regulars, bring in forty people.

26
00:01:04,739 --> 00:01:05,651
Step three.

27
00:01:05,651 --> 00:01:06,551
Selection.

28
00:01:06,454 --> 00:01:08,555
Each one makes a cup of chai.

29
00:01:08,555 --> 00:01:09,884
That is the test.

30
00:01:10,234 --> 00:01:12,209
The best ten get an interview.

31
00:01:12,209 --> 00:01:13,707
Only two get the job.

32
00:01:14,057 --> 00:01:16,023
So recruitment is positive.

33
00:01:16,023 --> 00:01:17,390
It attracts many.

34
00:01:17,390 --> 00:01:19,025
Selection is negative.

35
00:01:19,025 --> 00:01:20,339
It rejects many.

36
00:01:20,989 --> 00:01:22,005
Step four.

37
00:01:22,005 --> 00:01:24,026
Placement and orientation.

38
00:01:24,376 --> 00:01:28,815
Each helper gets the right job, and
on day one, Meena shows them around.

39
00:01:29,465 --> 00:01:31,659
Recruitment can look in two places.

40
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:34,849
Internal sources are
people already inside.

41
00:01:34,849 --> 00:01:37,761
Meena herself moved up to run this outlet.

42
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:41,050
External sources are
new people from outside.

43
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:43,375
They bring fresh skills and ideas.

44
00:01:44,025 --> 00:01:46,617
Then come the four steps
that keep good people.

45
00:01:46,967 --> 00:01:47,867
Training.

46
00:01:47,744 --> 00:01:51,477
Asha teaches her recipe, so
every cup tastes the same.

47
00:01:51,827 --> 00:01:52,727
Appraisal.

48
00:01:52,664 --> 00:01:55,908
A regular review of how
well each person works.

49
00:01:56,258 --> 00:01:57,857
Promotion and transfer.

50
00:01:57,857 --> 00:02:01,509
A star moves up, or moves
across to a busier outlet.

51
00:02:01,859 --> 00:02:03,110
And compensation.

52
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:06,113
Fair pay and rewards, so good people stay.

53
00:02:06,763 --> 00:02:09,313
So what does staffing
look like at work today?

54
00:02:09,663 --> 00:02:11,031
Manpower planning.

55
00:02:11,031 --> 00:02:14,964
A hospital plans how many
nurses each night shift needs.

56
00:02:15,314 --> 00:02:16,263
Recruitment.

57
00:02:16,263 --> 00:02:20,488
A company visits colleges to meet
students before they graduate.

58
00:02:20,838 --> 00:02:21,738
Selection.

59
00:02:21,586 --> 00:02:24,533
A bank runs a written
test, then an interview.

60
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:25,783
Training.

61
00:02:25,631 --> 00:02:29,844
A new call centre agent sits beside
an expert for the first week.

62
00:02:30,194 --> 00:02:31,094
Appraisal.

63
00:02:30,987 --> 00:02:34,803
Each year, a manager and an
employee review goals together.

64
00:02:35,453 --> 00:02:37,975
But does careful staffing always work?

65
00:02:37,975 --> 00:02:39,051
Not perfectly.

66
00:02:39,401 --> 00:02:40,389
The good side.

67
00:02:40,389 --> 00:02:43,746
The right fit, fewer people
quitting, and better service.

68
00:02:44,096 --> 00:02:45,133
The hard side.

69
00:02:45,133 --> 00:02:48,914
It takes time and money, and
good people can still be missed.

70
00:02:49,264 --> 00:02:53,186
Interviewers also tend to pick
people who are like themselves.

71
00:02:53,186 --> 00:02:54,258
That is bias.

72
00:02:54,608 --> 00:02:56,925
One fix is a structured interview.

73
00:02:56,925 --> 00:02:59,493
The same questions, for every person.

74
00:02:59,843 --> 00:03:06,012
In 2022, a large review of hiring research
found it predicted job performance

75
00:03:06,012 --> 00:03:06,912
best.

76
00:03:07,084 --> 00:03:08,737
So the lesson is simple.

77
00:03:08,737 --> 00:03:11,259
Hire with care, then help people grow.

78
00:03:11,909 --> 00:03:12,817
Quick check.

79
00:03:12,817 --> 00:03:16,133
Forty people apply, and Ravi
turns away thirty eight.

80
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:17,960
Which step turned them away?

81
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:20,760
Selection!

82
00:03:20,606 --> 00:03:23,214
It picks the best, and rejects the rest.

83
00:03:23,814 --> 00:03:24,827
So, remember.

84
00:03:25,127 --> 00:03:29,237
Staffing means filling jobs with the
right people, and keeping them filled.

85
00:03:29,587 --> 00:03:33,600
Plan, recruit, select, place,
train, appraise, promote, and pay.

86
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,651
Recruitment attracts many.

87
00:03:35,651 --> 00:03:37,313
Selection picks the few.

88
00:03:37,913 --> 00:03:42,593
Next time, Ravi learns to guide his team,
and make all their work fit together.
